From: so1_sanctum <so1_sanctum@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:39:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ptlc: a swap on two key locks with single-signer adaptor
 signatures

Two BIP340 entries, each locked to a key of its maker and each naming the
other party as its destination, are a swap with one adaptor pre-signature
each way: no two-party key, and neither the secret nor its point on the
chain. The fixed destination is what makes one key enough, since the key's
owner can then sign only to pay the counterparty.

Tests on the mock chain: the swap in the four parity cases of key and
nonce, the pre-signature and the lock keys opening nothing else, both ways
of abandoning it, the late claim that gives the secret away, and the same
swap with a zero destination, which the first party takes back.

No contract change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
